{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell","id":353085,"title":"Wound's Realm is the Hell?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-28T13:48:52-08:00","id":353085,"title":"Wound's Realm is the Hell?","content":"Mine Sweden game about fight with Bale Hounds pack in Lapland is going to the end. As one of major plotlines is that Bale Hounds cultivating Wound Locus under local church, for the final I want to get them to the &quot;hell&quot; - Wound Realm the Locus leads to - and let the PCs to close it, once and for all. The only problem I have is this - <b>How does Wound Realm looks like? </b>Is it like Inferno's Hell ( that is not mentioned even in book )? Or is it more like <a href=\"http://silenthill.wikia.com/wiki/Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Silent's Hill Otherworld</a>? Any ideas on this in 1ed materials? I assume it's one of Places-That-Should-Not-Be in 2ed Forsaken?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T15:01:31-08:00","id":353164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell#post353085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume it's one of Places-That-Should-Not-Be in 2ed Forsaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much.<br /> <br /> It's a bad place. You can make it appear however you want.<br /> <br /> Somewhere, I believe in <i>Lore of the Forsaken</i>, it describes it as the place where Father Wolf was slain, with at least one of the Maeljin setting up their home right on top of his remains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-28-2014, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T22:33:16-08:00","id":353507,"title":"","content":"The first wound is father wolfs death location, with the maeljin of... violence i think being the one to gain supreme power from it. I may be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T14:32:33-08:00","id":354097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell?p=353507#post353507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first wound is father wolfs death location, with the maeljin of... violence i think being the one to gain supreme power from it. I may be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never understood how that legend crept up. The Firstborn/Forsaken, for all intents and purposes, acted in accordance with their nature when they did that. I've always viewed it as the failure of them to live up to the duty that they inherited that allow wounds and Maeljin to fester. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T15:45:52-08:00","id":354137,"title":"","content":"Well the legend says that Thurifuge was originally a minor spirit of violence that subsisted upon the cycle of hunting among beasts and spirits. When Urfarah was laid low it was an act of such unprecedented violence as to elevate Thurifuge to the rank of Incarna. Supposedly he's constructed his palace upon (or with) the bones of Urfarah at the First Wound, the location where he was murdered. <br /> <br /> I remember it fairly well, but upon searching I can't find it so I might just be completely insane. I recall there being an implication that the killing blow to Urfarah was done by one of the First Pack not out of duty, but out of murderous desire. They may or may not have been the first Bale Hound and/or Soulless Wolf depending on how you interpret Viruhk-Ur's existence. That said even if my brain decided to just make that up, Soulless Wolf is a (probable) second strong link between the Uratha, the Maeljin, and Urfarah.<br /> <br /> As for Wounds themselves, there are some rules for them starting on page 58 of Lore of the Forsaken. I think they'd look physically like a really fucked up part of the Shadow, which I always imagined was like in Silent Hill when it transitions from Double Hell to Scarytown.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://art.penny-arcade.com/photos/494733791_vSJvi/0/1050x10000/494733791_vSJvi-1050x10000.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T17:55:14-08:00","id":354207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell?p=354097#post354097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Never understood how that legend crept up. The Firstborn/Forsaken, for all intents and purposes, acted in accordance with their nature when they did that. I've always viewed it as the failure of them to live up to the duty that they inherited that allow wounds and Maeljin to fester.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take Therifuge's tittle as Architect of Violence into consideration. Up until that point, that was an action of violence without precedence. So much, that it broke the world, dividing it into Hisil and Gurihal. We're talking about the Incarnae who feed off World Wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T21:57:23-08:00","id":354450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell?p=354137#post354137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the legend says that Thurifuge was originally a minor spirit of violence that subsisted upon the cycle of hunting among beasts and spirits. When Urfarah was laid low it was an act of such unprecedented violence as to elevate Thurifuge to the rank of Incarna. Supposedly he's constructed his palace upon (or with) the bones of Urfarah at the First Wound, the location where he was murdered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not have Hound of Thurifuge in game, but maybe interesting would that Hounds of Deadly Sins, in reality, served him, and connect to his realm with Mother of Wolves remains?<br /> <br /> Amd about alternative - the Realm governed by Seven Deadly Sins? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell?p=354137#post354137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember it fairly well, but upon searching I can't find it so I might just be completely insane. I recall there being an implication that the killing blow to Urfarah was done by one of the First Pack not out of duty, but out of murderous desire. They may or may not have been the first Bale Hound and/or Soulless Wolf depending on how you interpret Viruhk-Ur's existence. That said even if my brain decided to just make that up, Soulless Wolf is a (probable) second strong link between the Uratha, the Maeljin, and Urfarah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if it is fanon, it's extrtemly cool and logical, thanks for idea! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell?p=354137#post354137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Wounds themselves, there are some rules for them starting on page 58 of Lore of the Forsaken. I think they'd look physically like a really fucked up part of the Shadow, which I always imagined was like in Silent Hill when it transitions from Double Hell to Scarytown.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so Otherworld Silent Hill it is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T03:07:27-08:00","id":354639,"title":"","content":"For me, the Otherworld is kinda how I have the Shadow on a <i>good </i>day. I haven't actually had anyone go through a Wound yet in any of my games so haven't had to figure out what exactly the connected realm would look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T03:28:53-08:00","id":354653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell?p=354639#post354639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, the Otherworld is kinda how I have the Shadow on a <i>good </i>day. I haven't actually had anyone go through a Wound yet in any of my games so haven't had to figure out what exactly the connected realm would look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would rather go with <a href=\"http://silenthill.wikia.com/wiki/Fog_World\" target=\"_blank\">Fog World Silent Hill</a> as general Shadow Realm feel. It is spooky, it is sometimes more concealed, but it looks as &quot;other side&quot; of mirror to Material Realm. The Wounds would very much look like totally Otherworld Silent Hill - at least in town and cities.<br /> <br /> Thing is - I have small town on the edge of Lapland where the action of chronicle take place. Normally I would be on whole &quot;rust, chains, and mutilated bodies in darkness&quot; for Wound here, like SH Otherworld. But what could be more &quot;primal&quot; suited for theme of desecrated Wound Realm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-30-2014, 06:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T11:26:05-08:00","id":354917,"title":"","content":"Fog World fails to encapsulate the Hisil viscerality and variance and sheer alieness, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T11:35:37-08:00","id":354924,"title":"","content":"I will quote a little paragraph from 1ed corebook about Shadow Realm here then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>A WALK THROUGH THE SHADOW</b><br /> The Shadow Realm clearly re\ufb02ects its earthly counterpart, but even at \ufb01rst glance, the re\ufb02ection is<br /> somewhat\u2026 different. The landscape is much the same. The trees are in the same places; the time of day seems the same. The colors seem peculiar \u2014 the way the sky changes color just before a storm. Animals make their way through the plants, but something is different about them. The trees cast longer shadows, and their branches wave like sign language. Some of the shapes of the plants and animals are almost stylized or slightly abstract \u2014 others seem sharper around the edges. Many of the animals have an intelligence in their eyes that\u2019s equal to but unlike a human\u2019s \u2014 one wedded to strange instinct. The air feels crisper, clearer, with scents both familiar and unfamiliar, which are never quite so strong in the physical world. The power that subtly hums through the shadow world makes you feel more vital, more alive somehow. It\u2019s as if the world is whispering for you to take to all fours and hunt \u2014 or to run.<br /> It doesn\u2019t matter if the sun or the moon is in the sky, because their faces are at least partially hidden by<br /> cloud. There\u2019s a tension in the air, a feeling that a storm is brewing and bad weather is coming. Occasionally<br /> storms do break \u2014 storms of strangely colored lightning and sheets of rain that fall in odd patterns \u2014 but much<br /> of the time the atmosphere maintains a steady feel of unsettled weather. <br /> Then you notice the strangest omission. There are no people to be seen anywhere. Curious, you move on to the nearest town. Now the differences become more obvious. Some roads into the town are all but invisible. Others, those most heavily used, you realize, are brutal scars across the landscape. Traf\ufb01c moves across the roads, just as strangely off-kilter and subtly hostile as the rest of the world. Some of the cars are nothing but ghosts of themselves, insubstantial shadows passing along the blistering tarmac. Others are almost caricatures of themselves: monstrous SUVs thundering down the roads, pursued by predatory Porsche-spirits scattering lazy family sedans out of the way.<br /> The city itself is a disturbing sight. It spills out of its material world city limits, sending tendrils of brick and<br /> glass out into the surrounding countryside. For a moment, you get a sense of it as a predator in its own right, slowly preying on the landscape around it. As you walk down the street, the buildings are in a terrible jumble compared to their relative order in the physical world. Some are hardly visible, as insubstantial as some of the cars on the road. Other buildings seem larger than they do in the real world. An of\ufb01ce block looms overhead, obscuring the light all around it. You feel an ethereal yet heavy pressure and fatigue as you pass it. Another block burns with lights and, as you approach, you hear the sounds of anxious delight and half-clear music. It\u2019s a bar, a favored meeting place for the local youth in the physical world, and a beacon in the spirit world. </div> </div> </div>From what I read here you only need to change &quot;brewing storm&quot; for &quot;bound by fog&quot; and you got Fog World Silent Hill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T11:45:12-08:00","id":354927,"title":"","content":"... No, Fog obscures things. I want my players to see exactly how tree spirits use their roots to whip around other, lesser plant spirits and cannibalize them with a mouth made of vines not unlike an octopus, and how they communicate when wind rings along it's foliage spelling First Tongue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T12:10:15-08:00","id":354952,"title":"","content":"I tend to run the normal Shadow as Otherworld, wounds are likely to be worse, and I run Werewolf in Detroit &lt;_&lt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T12:42:45-08:00","id":355029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell?p=354952#post354952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to run the normal Shadow as Otherworld, wounds are likely to be worse, and I run Werewolf in Detroit &lt;_&lt;</div> </div> </div> </div>In my headcanon? Detroit is like the Mecca of the Lodge of Ruin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T21:11:38-08:00","id":358005,"title":"","content":"Half a city without street lights. Dead buildings and cracked streets are scattered like pockmarks through a corpse. Motown is strangling, spiritually and physically. Over three hundred homicides a year and seventy percent go unsolved. It\u2019s a great place to hide if you\u2019re a monster. This is not the quiet existential death that the Lodge of Ruin embraces, this is a city dying of starvation and violence.<br /> <br /> Spirits of death roll among machines and ancient hatreds, down corridors wracked with screaming flesh. Building spirits howl as they are denied precious life in the form of upkeep and electricity. Great worms like garden eels rise higher than skyscrapers, boiling out of cracks where the city has denied lights to the streets. Every so often, one will curl down ever so slowly and swallow up a growing chunk of the spiritual city and drag it back up into the Shadow sky, chewing it to shreds and swallowing, at which the city around it begins to reconstitute. Massive beings, like circling sharks, dart in to snag fallen pieces of spiritual detritus and jet back out again. Spine-covered centipedes and beasts capable of tearing human-sized holes in the gauntlet scurry back and forth, capturing human and ghost alike, yanking them out of Twilight or even from the physical world. Scattered with poorly-healed pockmarks, the thin state of the Gauntlet would be a terrible thing anywhere else; here it is just the icing on the cake. It is an even more dangerous place for mortal, Uratha, and spirit alike than the Shadow elsewhere in the world, and strangely, the Gauntlet is even thinner than usual. It is an angry, terrible, polluted place where spirits run rampant and unchecked. It is no longer a hunting ground, it is a killing floor and possession factory.<br /> <br /> In the physical world, spirit-claimed wander the streets openly and many even claim to know of and be in charge of their otherworldly riders, actively hunting wolves or devouring the dead. They practice their own forms of magic, and even claim to have fused their souls and their spirit halves in some kind of monstrous mimicry of Uratha nature.<br /> <br /> When the Forsaken speak of their mistakes, they keep Detroit on their list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T22:55:13-08:00","id":358068,"title":"","content":"I knew my pack should have supported the America automobile industry more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T01:34:15-08:00","id":358127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell?p=358005#post358005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Over three hundred homicides a year and seventy percent go unsolved. It\u2019s a great place to hide if you\u2019re a monster. This is not the quiet existential death that the Lodge of Ruin embraces, this is a city dying of starvation and violence.<br /> (...)<br /> It is an even more dangerous place for mortal, Uratha, and spirit alike than the Shadow elsewhere in the world, and strangely, the Gauntlet is even thinner than usual. It is an angry, terrible, polluted place where spirits run rampant and unchecked. It is no longer a hunting ground, it is a killing floor and possession factory.<br /> <br /> In the physical world, spirit-claimed wander the streets openly and many even claim to know of and be in charge of their otherworldly riders, actively hunting wolves or devouring the dead. They practice their own forms of magic, and even claim to have fused their souls and their spirit halves in some kind of monstrous mimicry of Uratha nature.<br /> <br /> When the Forsaken speak of their mistakes, they keep Detroit on their list.</div> </div> </div> </div>You see, yourself pointed that Detroit is massive Wound in making, not typical Shadow Realm landscape. You also not marked typical <i>Otherwold Silent Hill</i> features, like chains, rust, barber and unpierced darkness enrolling everything.<br /> <br /> When I written about <i>Fog World Silent Hill</i>-like Hisil, I've mean on normal circumstances. And yes, mist is used only on special events - fog would probably been marking of thicker Gauntlet . My little town of Fell in northern Sweden has normal Shadow Realm, generally, <i>Silent Hill</i>-like, but clearly visible to any one seeing it - with weird looking monster-spirits from time to time and empty without any humans. You will not say to me that those creatues do not look like abstract and emotions spirits of Shadow Realm:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.translatedmemories.com/bookpgs/Pg26-27SH1Creature.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> But in the center of the city stands once church, now &quot;Gate to Hell&quot; - a Wound that is also a portal-in-making to the Wound Realm.<br /> <br /> How the Realm it's lead to should looked like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-03-2015, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T09:22:58-08:00","id":358370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell?p=358127#post358127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You also not marked typical <i>Otherwold Silent Hill</i> features, like chains, rust, barber and unpierced darkness enrolling everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume that's everywhere in the Shadow. In my write-up for my Geist and Forsaken players, I felt I didn't have to say &quot;oh, yeah, and the normal shadow stuff is here, too, so expect faceless representations of fears and junk, too.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's the <i>Shadow</i>, it's going to be dark and rusty and have lots of chains in there regardless.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T09:28:51-08:00","id":358374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is not the quiet existential death that the Lodge of Ruin embraces, this is a city dying of starvation and violence. </div> </div> </div>Wrong. That's exactly what the lodge embraces. The monuments rusting over, the lavish corridors and halls in forgotten hotels which had it's golden door handles stolen decades ago. The city where you either matter somehow or you're eaten alive by it. Ruins are alive as well. Rotting trees house billions of life-forms still.<br /> <br /> Generic death spirits? Fun. Pick the way it likes to see people die the most. Starvation spirits, death by exposure to the elements. Death by a knife to the throat, or a bottle shoved into an eye socket. The greatest ally for the Hunters in Darkness that not only survive, but thrive in this otherwise accurately named Hellhole is rust itself. The building spirit that starts to devour the other husks, growing too big to be hunted down are paralyzed by it. So are the factory line beasts, and the predatory vehicle choir. Everyone of their rituals involve the red marks, which reminds even spirits that they can bleed, too.<br /> <br /> The Rustbelt is a massive Shoal, with pockets of wounds. Because when you can't leave, you gotta have fun -somehow-.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 01-03-2015, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T09:53:14-08:00","id":358384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell?p=358370#post358370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that's everywhere in the Shadow. In my write-up for my Geist and Forsaken players, I felt I didn't have to say &quot;oh, yeah, and the normal shadow stuff is here, too, so expect faceless representations of fears and junk, too.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's the <i>Shadow</i>, it's going to be dark and rusty and have lots of chains in there regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>You read the fragment of the core I quoted, yes? It's basiclly states this:&quot;<i>Shadow</i> is a place that look like darker twin brother of Material World. Most streets are correct, buildings, things, animals. Only when it's not. The spirits prawn the empty streets from time to time. Some buildings have wrong number of corridors. And a like <b>subtle</b> changes.&quot;<br /> <br /> I could agree that Detroit's Shadow can be much more like the stuff you would find in Wound's Realm - chains, rust, etc. - but it more <b>exception</b>, than the typical state of <i>Hisil</i> - at least, according to the corebook. Your Detroit description goes in to &quot;this is very sick Shadow, on brink of becoming massive Wound&quot; I would asses.<br /> <br /> Really, when I read description of <i>Hisil</i> in supplements it much more <i>Fog Bound</i> than <i>Otherworld</i> Silent Hill feel I get ( minus mist, but I would use it for dense Gauntlet areas still ).<br /> <br /> <b>Side Note:</b> It's called <i>Shadow</i> not because it's rust and chains. It called because it's in symbiotic relation with Material Realm and it's mimic and reflects on it, and vice versa. It's ephemeral brother to Flesh Realm, not a predator to it. Best is to shown it on cosmology diagram.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://s7450.chomikuj.pl/ChomikImage.aspx?e=65NR2B3dRGhAofVZ55c3PLniivdDer_7y8unbaI8ZkioolYXyPdnRKxTuFLHJYQWZ8e4n3ZFXD_CNGp8U7t1Rdp6e8yMQx17Eu2fa9pazVE&amp;pv=2\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Wounds Realms, on the other hand, are totally <b>alien</b> to this ecology. In my games they are part of <b>Inferno</b>'s Hell, but devs has stated they are Places That Should Not Be in 2ed - and it means they are sub realms attached to <i>Shadow</i>, just like from <i>Hisil</i> you have Gates to Underworld or some weird Firstborn domains - like the Black Wolf's <i>Dark Forest</i>. <b>Wounds</b>, in reality, <b>are portals</b> to OTHER reality - in my games, <b>Inferno</b> in Lower Depths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-03-2015, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T10:13:41-08:00","id":358392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;<i>Shadow</i> is a place that look like darker twin brother of Material World. Most streets are correct, buildings, things, animals. Only when it's not. The spirits prawn the empty streets from time to time. Some buildings have wrong number of corridors. And a like <b>subtle</b> changes.&quot; </div> </div> </div>That's only at first glance.<br /> <br /> And your picture there isn't canon, or even close to being correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T10:16:18-08:00","id":358394,"title":"","content":"Er, that cosmology diagram is wildly inaccurate at best, and flat-out wrong in various ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T12:40:28-08:00","id":358524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell?p=358392#post358392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's only at first glance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Show me were in books is described &quot;second&quot; glance, then, so I could get it also better grip on Shadow. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell?p=358392#post358392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And your picture there isn't canon, or even close to being correct.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell?p=358394#post358394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er, that cosmology diagram is wildly inaccurate at best, and flat-out wrong in various ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the closest to the &quot;official cosmology made in to diagram&quot; I get in 10 years on new World of Darkness. Having better fit, show me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T20:58:30-08:00","id":358802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell?p=358524#post358524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the closest to the &quot;official cosmology made in to diagram&quot; I get in 10 years on new World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also positively <i>ancient</i>, being &quot;current&quot; back in the time of Mage.<br /> <br /> Mage came out in late 2005. You may recall that nWoD started in 2004.<br /> <br /> Your &quot;diagram&quot; was out of date six games and a decade ago.<br /> <br /> (It also needs rehosting, like literally any image you plan on hotlinking. Dropbox is good for this.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having better fit, show me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>It's rather difficult to meaningfully diagram television static. Everything has ways into everything else.<br /> <br /> The Shadow reflects and feeds off of the Essence generated by memory and emotion in the Flesh, distorting along symbolic lines with high levels of unchecked spiritual activity and along perceptual lines in the absence of regular human presence. Some parts of the Shadow reflect the Flesh on a ratio greater than 1:1, resulting in Places-That-Aren't from expanding the metaphysical contents of a location. These places are still in Shadow, but are not to be confused with places reached through supernatural passageways from Shadow to elsewhere. The Gauntlet is more involved than &quot;veil between worlds,&quot; but difficult to get a good look at \u2014 Dave's said more information will be presented in the 2e corebook, which has been out of the writing stage for several weeks as of the time of this writing.<br /> <br /> The Underworld sustains ghosts through Essence generated by the remembrance of the dead, and the context of earthbound ghosts' anchors are usually emotional and act as a grounding mechanism by which they remember who they were; being spiritlike remnants of humans (who have no direct spiritual reflection, remember), ghosts are not exactly sane by spiritual standards (Geist's notes that they taste awful, combined with the fact that even ghosts with only a singular emotional context anchoring their identities can evince humanlike behavior if they're still sapient, suggests that the law of appropriate consumption means spirits aren't going to want to touch the Essence ghosts feed on unless their concept allows for it or something's gone pear-shaped). The Shadow appears to have laws in place that treat the Underworld something like a prison, and portals from Shadow to the Great Below are unlike those that lead between the lands of the living and the dead in that they're always open.<br /> <br /> The Lower Depths are not strictly an actual thing, being an umbrella term for any number of unreal worlds that prey on the world(s) of phenomena and consume and/or corrupt the things they lack; some of these beings, like the Maeljin and their servants, find their way into the Shadow and run afoul of werewolves.<br /> <br /> Only the worst Wounds become dense enough to warp metaphysical space and permit a Hellmouth to form, much as loci are not innately intersections between worlds so much as they are points of easy passage. Of course, the trouble with this is that, like any locus, Wounds gradually warp the spirits around them to be more in line with their resonance, which by design eventually results in more atrocities being committed around the place until the Wound has festered enough to bring Hell close to the surface.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T00:57:55-08:00","id":358907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell?p=358802#post358802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also positively <i>ancient</i>, being &quot;current&quot; back in the time of Mage.<br /> <br /> Mage came out in late 2005. You may recall that nWoD started in 2004.<br /> <br /> Your &quot;diagram&quot; was out of date six games and a decade ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not think it's that bad, as it is only &quot;shorthand&quot; to draw basic various Realms &quot;intersections&quot;. Probably there are more detail diagrams there ( if someone could draw cosmology so complex ), but this one is great as &quot;weird Mysterium teacher shows a neophyte quick glimps of cosmos&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell?p=358802#post358802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(It also needs rehosting, like literally any image you plan on hotlinking. Dropbox is good for this.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Tried for weeks now to use Dropbox, but could not get it work for graphics on this forum engine. Got any results on this? And hints on this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell?p=358802#post358802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's rather difficult to meaningfully diagram television static. Everything has ways into everything else.<br /> (And rest)</div> </div> </div> </div>I get those, really. Still, how this simple cosmological diagram is wrong in this context? Conceptually, those realms are exactly were picture put's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T01:14:15-08:00","id":358909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell?p=358907#post358907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get those, really. Still, how this simple cosmological diagram is wrong in this context? Conceptually, those realms are exactly were picture put's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Astral is absolutely not disconnected from the Shadow and the Underworld is absolutely not separated from the material realm by the Shadow or even the Gauntlet, to point to the most glaring errors committed in the name of stylization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T01:31:42-08:00","id":358915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/353085-wound-s-realm-is-the-hell?p=358909#post358909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Astral is absolutely not disconnected from the Shadow and the Underworld is absolutely not separated from the material realm by the Shadow or even the Gauntlet, to point to the most glaring errors committed in the name of stylization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tis the problem with the effort of trying to depict a system that may be 3 to more dimensions upon a 2d area. <br /> <br /> Tempted to wonder if it would be better served to see WoD as something akin to the Marvel multiverse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:",